@bank dept:works
// Head writer 5: clock-in remarks, for the Career engineer's clock-in/out panel on the Works bay wall (claude/leave).
// Co-workers in the bay say one as you clock in or out. Keys (the Career engineer's, 2026-10-17):
// clock.in (start of day), clock.out (end of day), clock.monday (clocking in on a Monday: your weekend),
// clock.friday (clocking out on a Friday: weekend plans), clock.back (first shift back from leave or sick).
// Shift 09:00-17:00 (playtest 1), tea and biscuits at 13:00, your days off are Sat-Sun. Not everyone in Works is off at the weekend, so shared
// lines ask about YOUR weekend and never claim the speaker's. One short line each, readable on a phone.

== clock.in
- {hi}, {nick}. Board's full this morning. Pick a good one.
- Morning. Kettle's on in the tea corner, if you're quick.
- Nine o'clock. Somebody should do something about nine o'clock.   #funny
- There's a scrubber on the board with your name on it. Not literally.
- {hi}. Tea's at one. Hold on till then.
- Clocked in? Good. The fans on Five are humming again.
- Another day, another filter. {hi}, {nick}.
- You look awake. How? Tell me how.   #funny
- Quiet night, the night lot say. Let's keep it that way.
- {hi}. Grab a job before the Chief gives you one.
- Bay smells of oil and toast. Someone ate breakfast in here.   #funny
- Mind the panel by the racks. It sticks. It always sticks.
- First job's always the hardest. After that it's just the day.
- Saw the stars on the way down. Nice start, that.
- {hi}. Night shift left us a note. Mostly crossed out.   #funny
- I'm here. My eyes aren't yet. Give them an hour.   #funny
- Board's light today. Don't tell it I said so.
- Morning. Gloves are back on the hook. Somebody tidied.
? tier>=friend
- Oh good, it's you. The day just got easier.   #warm
- Saved you the good spanner. Don't say I never do anything.   #warm
? time:afternoon
- Afternoon start? Lucky. You missed the morning rush.

== clock.out
- Five o'clock. That's us. {bye}.
- Good day, that. Nothing caught fire. Nothing even smoked.   #funny
- Off you go, {nick}. Dinner's on till half eight.
- Clocked out. The board can wait till morning.
- That's the day done. My feet have opinions.   #funny
- Nice work today. The bay sounds right.
- Off to the mess. If there's stew, I'm having two.
- Done. Shower before the hot water goes, that's my plan.
- {bye}, {nick}. Leave the scrubbers to dream.
- Long one. Good one, though.
- Hang your gloves up or the Chief will notice. She notices.
- Evening, then. Anything on tonight?
- Off you go. Tomorrow's jobs aren't going anywhere.
- I'm going to sit down and not fix anything for hours.   #funny
- Same time tomorrow. Bring your good mood back.
- Today was a tea-break day. Some days the tea is the high point.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Good shift with you, {nick}. Same again tomorrow?   #warm
- Save me a seat at dinner if you get there first.
? mood:low
- Rough one. Tomorrow's a fresh board.
? cue:repair.you@dept
- You fixed it today. I heard it start up. Lovely sound.   #warm

== clock.monday
- Monday. {hi}. Good weekend?
- Back again! Did you get any rest, or did the ship keep you busy?
- {hi}, {nick}. Do anything nice at the weekend?
- Weekend go all right? You look like you slept.
- Monday morning. Tell me something good from the weekend.
- How was the weekend? Garden, gym, or bunk?   #funny
- Monday. The board missed you. Well, it's longer, anyway.   #funny
- Good to see you. Weekend's always too short, isn't it?
- {hi}. Did you call home at the weekend? All well?
- Back to it. Was the mess busy on Sunday? Bread day.
? tier>=friend
- There you are. Quiet bay without you, Monday or not.   #warm
- I want the whole weekend. Every bit. At tea, mind.   #warm

== clock.friday
- Friday! Two days off for you. Any plans?
- That's the week. {bye}, {nick}. Enjoy the weekend.
- Off for two days? Rest. Properly. No fixing anything.
- Weekend plans? Bunk counts as a plan.   #funny
- Friday. Music jam tonight, if you fancy it.
- Have a good weekend. Don't let anyone hand you a spanner.   #funny
- The week's done. Go and do something that isn't filters.
- Enjoy your days off. The bay will still be here Monday.
- Going to the garden at the weekend? It's lovely on a rest day.
- Two days off. Sleep in. Hot water's yours before the rush.
? tier>=friend
- Have a good one, {nick}. Tell me all about it Monday.   #warm

== clock.back
- You're back! Good to see you, {nick}.   #warm
- Welcome back. Bay wasn't the same.   #warm
- {hi}. Feeling better? Take it easy today.   #warm
- Look who's back. The board's been asking after you.   #funny
- There you are. Kettle's on. Ease in.   #warm
- Back with us! Your gloves are where you left them.
- Good to have you back. Pick an easy one to start.
- Welcome back, {nick}. You were missed. Properly.   #warm
? tier>=friend
- Oh, you're back. I've saved up all the gossip.   #warm
- Missed you on the bay. Don't do that again. Well, do, if you need to.   #warm

== clock.late
// Gentle teasing when you clock in after 09:00.
- Afternoon! Oh, sorry. It just felt like afternoon.   #funny
- There you are. The board ate two jobs while you were out.   #funny
- Lie-in? Don't let the Chief see the clock.   #funny
- Late one. Grab a job, quick, look busy.   #funny
- Morning, {nick}. Well. Most of it's still morning.   #funny
- Hot water ran out, did it? Happens to us all.   #funny
- The kettle waited for you. It's that kind of kettle.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Saved you a job. Not a good one. You were late.   #funny

== clock.early
// Clocking out well before the end of the shift (before 15:00). Gentle, never a telling-off.
- Off already? Hope all's well.
- Short day? Fair enough.
- Heading off? Look after yourself.
- Early one. The board will keep. Go on.
- Off you go. We'll hold the fort.
- All right? Shout if you need anything.   #warm
- Early finish. Rest up, if that's what it is.
? tier>=friend
- Off early? Find me at dinner if you want company.   #warm
